  "chunks": [
    {
      "id": "chunk-cheap-fpv-motors-for-antweight-weapons",
      "title": "Cheap FPV motors as antweight weapon motors: what the database should compare",
      "section": "Weapons",
      "weight_classes": [
        "fairyweight",
        "antweight",
        "plastic-antweight"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "weapon-motor",
        "fpv",
        "budget",
        "mad",
        "t-motor",
        "emax",
        "iflight"
      ],
      "entity_refs": [
        "motor-mad-bsc2207-5",
        "motor-mad-fs2004-dynamo",
        "motor-tmotor-f1507-2700kv",
        "motor-tmotor-f2004-1700kv",
        "motor-iflight-xing-e-pro-2207",
        "motor-emax-eco-ii-2207",
        "motor-betafpv-1805"
      ],
      "sources": [
        "https://store.mad-motor.com/collections/fpv-motor",
        "https://store.tmotor.com/categorys/f-series-racing-motor",
        "https://shop.iflight.com/xing-e-pro-2207-2-6s-fpv-nextgen-motor-pro874",
        "https://shop.emax-usa.com/collections/diy/products/eco-ii-2207-brushless-motor-1700kv-1900kv-2400kv",
        "https://betafpv.com/products/1805-brushless-motors"
      ],
      "body_md": "Cheap FPV motors can be excellent antweight value, but the database should not compare them only by KV. **Mass and stator size** tell you roughly how much motor you are buying; **shaft diameter and bell retention** matter directly to impact survival; **winding resistance and manufacturer peak current** help compare electrical stress; and **cell rating/KV** determine how much reduction is needed to reach a sane weapon RPM. Drone peak-current and power figures come from propeller tests and should not be treated as continuous combat ratings. Purpose-built combat motors usually spend extra mass/cost on shafts, bearings, retention, mounting, or mechanical support rather than magically having better KV. For budget builds, a $10 MAD BSC 2207.5 or $13 EMAX ECO II can be compelling if the weapon is belt-driven and the motor is physically protected; for very light builds, 12xx-15xx T-Motors save substantial mass. A larger 5mm-shaft iFlight 2207 may be mechanically attractive even when it is heavier."
    }
  ]
